@startuml
title BridgeIT - Data Flow Diagram

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Business Stakeholder /\nRequirements Engineer" as User

rectangle "Web Frontend" as UI
rectangle "FastAPI Adapter" as API
rectangle "Application Use Cases" as App
rectangle "Requirement Domain Model" as Domain
database "SQLite\nrequirements table" as DB
rectangle "AIGateway" as AIGateway
cloud "Google Gemini API" as Gemini

User --> UI : requirement text /\nrequirement id /\nhuman decision

UI --> API : HTTP + JSON

API --> App : validated request data

App --> Domain : create / analyse /\nclarify / validate / reject

Domain --> App : requirement id,\ntext, lifecycle status

App --> DB : save / retrieve\nid + text + status
DB --> App : persisted requirement

App --> AIGateway : requirement text
AIGateway --> Gemini : analysis request
Gemini --> AIGateway : AI response
AIGateway --> App : AIAnalysis\nquality indication + issues

App --> API : operation result
API --> UI : JSON response
UI --> User : requirement state /\nquality feedback

note bottom of DB
Only the current requirement
id, text and status are persisted.
AIAnalysis is not persisted.
end note

@enduml
